sections.text:
In these Rules unless the context otherwise requires:
(a) ‘Act’ means the Family Courts Act, 1984;
(b) ‘Citizen of India’ means such person, who is or is deemed to be a Citizen of India under part-II of the Constitution of India;
(c) ‘Governor’ means the Governor of Jharkhand;
(d) ‘Government’ means the Government of Jharkhand;
(e) ‘High Court’ means the High Court of Jharkhand, Ranchi;
(f) ‘Post’ means the Post of Judge;
(g) ‘Section’ means the Section of the Family Courts Act, 1984;
(h) Words and expressions used but not defined in these Rules shall have the same meanings which may have been assigned to them in the Family Courts Act, 1984.
